ates and Canada. The firm adhere to rigorous underwriting and investing criteria centered on key industry, property and tenant level cash flow standards. The firm believe their focused approach provides a competitive advantage and the potential for stable and attractive returns. EPR Properties was established on August 22, 1997 and is based in Kansas City, United States.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gregory K. Silvers J.D. | President, CEO & Board Chair | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 54 people. Revenue per employee of $13.3M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $5.0M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $284K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["EPR Properties is a mid-cap real estate business with a $4.6B market cap on $718M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $269M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 37 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.53\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.9\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3247462.85},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 35% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 38% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","28 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Agilyx: GreenDot to acquire 50% of French packaging EPR company Lko, expanding its European recycling platform","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/agilyx-greendot-to-acquire-50-of-french-packaging-epr-company-leko-expanding-its-european-recycling-platform-302930721.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793882520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Is EPR Properties (EPR) A Bargain Following Raised Guidance And A Higher Dividend?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-epr/epr-properties/news/is-epr-properties-epr-a-bargain-following-raised-guidance-an","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793878437.762,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.971,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance","dividend"]},{"title":"How to Build $5,450 a Month in Tax-Free Dividend Income Inside a Roth IRA","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/build-5-450-month-tax-181911000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793989957.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.665,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"3 Ways to Cash In on the Multiplex Turnaround No One Saw Coming","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/3-ways-cash-multiplex-turnaround-171717000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793899661.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.153,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The IRS Taxes These 5 High-Yield REIT Dividends as Ordinary Income (Unless You Move Them)","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/irs-taxes-5-high-yield-143252000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793889927.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.382,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Six Flags Entertainment Corporation Reports 2026 Third Quarter Results","sour