runs 35pp above the Real Estate median (23%), a real cost or pricing edge over peers.","It captures 2.89x its revenue share in sector profits, taking a disproportionate slice of the profit pool.","It accounts for 0.2% of sector revenue and 0.6% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been gaining share of the sector profit pool (+39.5% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 145 companies in the universe; the top four hold 25% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted higher, up 19% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 8% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 22% and a beta of 0.77, it is more defensive than the market.","About $43.6M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 81% in the 2020 crash, 36% in the 2022 bear market and 78% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 38% below its DCF fair value of $96.24, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 40%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $68.11 to $137 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Real Estate peers: P/E 16.8 vs 23.6 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 16% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 5.9% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 11 covering analysts target $63.77 on average, 7% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 6% falls short of the cost of capital of 7.1%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have been steady (CV 0.29).","It converts 37% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.53x.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 37%.","ROE of 12% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.4x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 10pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 4.9x net debt to EBITDA ($90.6M of cash against $2.9B of debt), with interest covered 3.1x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.18 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 3.0% over 3 years, 11.6% over 5 years and 5.5% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 15%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 58.9% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 45.2% a year over five years.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 21.1% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 47, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.3%, and institutions hold 85%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (13 sales, net $3.2M sold).","It returns 6.6% a year to shareholders (0.2% in buybacks and 6.3% in dividends).","It pays out 103% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk.","Short interest is elevated at 13.6% of the float, 8.5 days to cover."],"people":["With about 54 employees, each generates about $13.3M of revenue, 5.8x the Real Estate median, and productivity has risen 5.7% a year.","That works out to $5.0M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.6M (0x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $284K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":68,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but it earns less than its cost of capital.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 49, gates 12/26)","Trades 38% below fair value of $96.24","FCF margin 37.5%","Revenue grew 11.6%/yr over 5y","P/E 16.8x vs sector 23.6x"],"cons":["ROIC 6.0% vs WACC 7.1%","Net debt/EBITDA